# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# What omamobile-ingot-firmware copies from the Saga's own modem_a
# partition (a FAT file system holding Qualcomm's image/ tree) into the
# firmware search path. Data, not code: the tool reads it and refuses a
# line it can't parse. Nothing named here is in the repository or the
# package; every file comes from the user's own phone.
#
#   source-glob|destination|note
#
# source-glob   a path relative to the partition root, matched without
#               regard to case; * and ? match any characters (also /).
#               It must match exactly one file: none is "missing", two or
#               more is "ambiguous", and either is reported and skipped
#               without stopping the others.
# destination   the absolute path to install to, directly inside
#               /usr/lib/firmware/qcom/sm8475/osom/ingot/ or
#               /usr/lib/firmware/updates/ath11k/WCN6855/hw2.1/. Anything
#               else is refused.
# note          free text, shown by `plan`.
#
# Several lines may name the same destination: they are alternatives, and
# the first whose source is found wins. A source ending in .mdt is a split
# image and is copied with its .b00, .b01, ... segments (from the same
# folder), renamed after the destination (a730_zap.mbn gets a730_zap.b00,
# which is the name the kernel's loader asks for). A destination named
# board-2.bin is not a copy: the source (the board data file) is wrapped
# in ath11k's board container under the name wifi_board_name.
#
# The source names are unconfirmed: they are the names Qualcomm images of
# this generation use, not yet read from a Saga. Run
# `omamobile-ingot-firmware plan` on the phone, which lists what it finds
# under image/, and correct the lines here (and drop this note) once the
# owner has confirmed them.

# The GPU's zap shader (the device tree asks msm for
# qcom/sm8475/osom/ingot/a730_zap.mbn). Unconfirmed: split or single.
image/a730_zap.mdt|/usr/lib/firmware/qcom/sm8475/osom/ingot/a730_zap.mbn|GPU zap shader, split image (installed under the .mbn name the DT asks for)
image/a730_zap.mbn|/usr/lib/firmware/qcom/sm8475/osom/ingot/a730_zap.mbn|GPU zap shader, single image

# The ADSP (battery through qcom_battmgr, audio): the DT asks the
# remoteproc for qcom/sm8475/osom/ingot/adsp.mdt. A single adsp.mbn loads
# under that name too (the loader reads the segments from the file itself
# when they are inside it). Unconfirmed: split or single.
image/adsp.mdt|/usr/lib/firmware/qcom/sm8475/osom/ingot/adsp.mdt|ADSP firmware, split image
image/adsp.mbn|/usr/lib/firmware/qcom/sm8475/osom/ingot/adsp.mdt|ADSP firmware, single image

# Wi-Fi: the WCN6855 hw2.1's mobile firmware, as overrides of
# linux-firmware's laptop files (the kernel reads firmware/updates/ first).
# Unconfirmed: the folder (image/ itself or a subfolder of it).
image/amss20.bin|/usr/lib/firmware/updates/ath11k/WCN6855/hw2.1/amss.bin|Wi-Fi firmware (the vendor's amss20.bin, as amss.bin)
image/*/amss20.bin|/usr/lib/firmware/updates/ath11k/WCN6855/hw2.1/amss.bin|Wi-Fi firmware, in a subfolder
image/m3.bin|/usr/lib/firmware/updates/ath11k/WCN6855/hw2.1/m3.bin|Wi-Fi M3 firmware
image/*/m3.bin|/usr/lib/firmware/updates/ath11k/WCN6855/hw2.1/m3.bin|Wi-Fi M3 firmware, in a subfolder
image/regdb.bin|/usr/lib/firmware/updates/ath11k/WCN6855/hw2.1/regdb.bin|Wi-Fi regulatory database
image/*/regdb.bin|/usr/lib/firmware/updates/ath11k/WCN6855/hw2.1/regdb.bin|Wi-Fi regulatory database, in a subfolder

# The Wi-Fi board data (calibration for this board's antennas), wrapped in
# board-2.bin. Once installed it hides linux-firmware's board-2.bin, which
# has no entry for the Saga, so the name must be the one ath11k looks for.
# Unconfirmed: the folder.
image/bdwlang.elf|/usr/lib/firmware/updates/ath11k/WCN6855/hw2.1/board-2.bin|Wi-Fi board data, wrapped as board-2.bin
image/*/bdwlang.elf|/usr/lib/firmware/updates/ath11k/WCN6855/hw2.1/board-2.bin|Wi-Fi board data, in a subfolder

# The board name ath11k looks for in board-2.bin. It comes from the chip
# (PCI ids, QMI chip and board ids) and the device tree's calibration
# variant, so it can't be known offline: empty here, and the board file
# is skipped until it is set. `plan` shows how to read it on the phone.
# Set it in /etc/omamobile/ingot-firmware.conf (wifi_board_name=...),
# which an update of this package leaves alone and which wins over this
# line.
wifi_board_name=
